  {"paper_ref": "Theorem 1.1", "lean_theorem": "distributionUniformExponential", "relation": "equivalent", "why": "c is universal and sits outside the ∀ over games. The hypotheses (nonempty A, B, ε>0, n≥1) and the bound match. The universe is restricted to Type 0, which is harmless."},
  {"paper_ref": "Quantum Parallel Repetition Conjecture", "lean_theorem": "standardQuantumParallelRepetition", "relation": "equivalent", "why": "Lean uses the standard 'C·exp(-cn)' form and includes n=0, which is trivial. This is qualitatively the same as the paper's form, with at most a negligible difference in how the constant is handled."}
